    "logo": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/7ab4963f9bacc76a0a31b94f8773cad5138d2dc3.png",
    "oneLiner": "The best cloud VMs for billions of agents",
    "longDescription": "**Problem**  Humans used to need laptops to do their work. Now they prompt agents instead, and those agents need computers too: always-on, in large quantities, and with unlimited capabilities.   Building and maintaining that yourself is far from trivial.  **Solution**  Box provides powerful, simple, permissive Ubuntu VMs in the cloud. In a box, an agent can work for long periods on code or on knowledge work like legal, research, reporting, and auditing.  **Why Box and not any other cloud VM?**  1. It is ready out of the box: every box ships with a desktop, chrome, languages, docker, snapshots, and templates, plus a CLI, SDK, API, and control pane for your fleet. 2. It is permissive and paradigm agnostic: any number of agents can use any number of boxes. Agents can run inside or use boxes as an external tool. 3. It is expertly crafted: we manage everything from the individual CPU to the orchestration software, which makes boxes stable, persistent, scalable, and secure. 4. It is the best",
